{"assumptions":["ASM-1/ASM-22: The 'Open Questions' section was not supplied; the questions raised in this run stand in for it, and any unresolved item goes into the estimate as an explicit assumption.","ASM-23: Effort is given in person-days per checklist item as a low/high range, with totals per section.","Q-8 over ASM-5: The ERP stock file is picked up daily, as the client stated; ASM-5's 'configurable frequency' is not estimated as a separate feature.","ASM-24/ASM-18: Volume is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.","ASM-25/ASM-19: Hosting is one cloud region in the client's cloud account.","ASM-13: Order and invoice records are kept indefinitely and never deleted before 7 years.","The intent artifact lists no span text, so spans I-1 to I-45 are mapped to the request in document order: I-1 is the estimation instruction, I-2 to I-43 are the checklist sections, I-44 is the technology stack and I-45 is the open-questions instruction.","Because the deliverable is a document, not running software, every acceptance criterion is a manual review of the delivered estimate or proposal file."],"critic":[{"finding":"AC-6.3 demands a separate QA 'Customer data-isolation testing' row with its own effort values, but AC-1.1/NFR-3 fix QA at exactly 12 rows, each named after a section-74 checklist item, so an extra row the checklist doesn't name breaks the count.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Staff manage companies but only admins manage users (Q-5), and nothing says how a new company's customer users get accounts (admin-only creation, staff request, or invitation), so the onboarding and permission path behind the 'User management' and 'Customer management' rows is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"ASM-8 blocks quantities above stock with a message, but nothing says whether that check applies to staff amendments or staff-created orders, so the over-stock path is undefined for the amendment and staff order rows.","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Cancellation and amendment both stop at dispatch and the invoice is created at dispatch, but no row covers correcting a dispatched or invoiced order (credit note, return or void), so the post-dispatch error path is missing from the estimate.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Risk tags include pii, yet keeping order and invoice records indefinitely (ASM-13) comes with no path for anonymising or erasing customer-user personal data, and no row or proposal section covers it.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-10.3's 'no row in the estimate depends on an open question that is missing from the list' can't be checked, because there's no reference list of open questions to compare against (ASM-1 says the section was never supplied).","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The estimate depends on volume (ASM-18/24), hosting (ASM-19/25), retention (ASM-13) and daily pickup (Q-8), but AC-10.1/10.2 don't list them, while AC-10.3 requires every unconfirmed dependency to appear, so the enumerated lists are incomplete against the AC's own rule.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The ERP pickup frequency is fixed at 'daily' in the scoped row, and the spec explicitly drops ASM-5's configurable frequency, so a schedule value that belongs in configuration is baked into the estimate.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-13.1 requires the proposal to name one specific cloud region, which hardcodes a deployment identifier that should be the client's configurable choice within their own account.","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-12.2 requires the proposal to name a backup approach, but backup isn't one of the 10 section-75 areas listed in REQ-11, which goes beyond the requested proposal scope.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"'Assumptions used' is never pinned to a defined set, and REQ-10 has its own numbered entries rather than ASM IDs, so a reviewer can't measure '100% cited by ID' against a fixed denominator.","reqId":"NFR-2","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"Difference between each section subtotal and the sum of its rows, and between the grand total and the sum of the 7 subtotals, is 0 person-days for both low and high values","text":"The estimate's totals reconcile exactly with its line items."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"100% of the 8 answers (Q-1 to Q-8) and of the assumptions used are cited by ID at least once in the estimate or proposal","text":"Every scoping decision in the estimate and proposal can be traced to a client answer or a stated assumption."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"81 of 81 section-74 checklist items appear as rows (0 missing)","text":"The estimate covers the full checklist."}],"outOfScope":["Building, configuring or deploying the first-release portal described in section 76; this run produces only the estimate and technology proposal (Q-1)","Online payment collection, payment gateways or card processing; payments are manual status tracking only (Q-2)","Roles inside a customer company, such as company admin or a buyer who needs approval (Q-4)","Customer users amending orders; only staff amend, and only before dispatch (Q-3)","Social login or single sign-on (ASM-4, ASM-27)","Migrating existing customers, products, price lists or past orders (ASM-17)","SMS or push notifications (ASM-15)","Custom report builder (ASM-16)","Languages other than English, and right-to-left layouts (ASM-30)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-1.1","level":"manual","then":"The count is Product/UX 8, Frontend 20, Backend 20, Integrations 5, QA 12, DevOps 10, Documentation 6, and each row's name matches a section-74 checklist item","when":"A reviewer counts the line items under each section heading"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-1.2","level":"manual","then":"Each is shown as its own row with its own effort value, not merged into one row","when":"A reviewer looks for the Frontend 'Authentication' item and the Backend 'Authentication' item"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-1.3","level":"manual","then":"No row's value is given only as a screen count or derived only from a screen count","when":"A reviewer checks how effort is expressed"}],"ears":"The estimate shall list each of the 81 items in the section-74 estimation checklist as its own line item under its section heading (Product/UX 8, Frontend 20, Backend 20, Integrations 5, QA 12, DevOps 10, Documentation 6), rather than estimating by screen count.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-3","I-4","I-5","I-6","I-7","I-8","I-9","I-10","I-11","I-12","I-13","I-14","I-15","I-16","I-17","I-18","I-19","I-20","I-21","I-22","I-23","I-24","I-25","I-26","I-27","I-28","I-29","I-30","I-31","I-32","I-33","I-34","I-35","I-36","I-37","I-38","I-39","I-40","I-41","I-42","I-43","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-2.1","level":"manual","then":"Every row shows a low value and a high value in person-days, and on every row the low value is less than or equal to the high value","when":"A reviewer reads each of the 81 rows"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-2.2","level":"manual","then":"Each section's low and high subtotal values equal the sums of that section's